  "notes": "The crossover pop-funk edge, and the tempo range is the widest in this batch for a documented reason: 78–96, because the signature record is slow and the party records sit at 92–96. ⚠ **`session.halfTime` is deliberately left false.** The research is precise — the backbeat is still on 2 and 4, and it only *reads* half-time because the kick pattern is halved. Setting `halfTime` would move the snare to beat 3 and produce a different record; the halving is authored where it belongs, in `kick.densityPerBar` 2–3 with `syncopation` at 0.12 and `offbeat8thShare` at 0.06, the least syncopated kick in this batch. \"A beat ticking time\" is `quantizeStrength` 0.95, `velocityVar` 0.08 and `swing` 0.51 — metronomic, and the only near-straight grid here. The harmony is the interpolated Stevie Wonder string cycle, so the `i–v–i–VI` family the research names carries weight 5 and the voicing register runs to 84 for strings over choir. ⚠ The choir is authored as `sustain_pad` at weight 4 in the countermelody because the research says explicitly that it is used as a chordal pad, not a hook; `octave_echo` and `answer_lick` sit under it so the layer keeps a reachable pool. ⚠ The bass is `mirror_kick` at `followRootsProb` 0.9 for the pedal the research names — sustained sub doubling the string root motion, minimal movement — rather than `reese_sustain`, which emits one note per chord and saturates. ⚠ `confidence` is `medium` per the research's high-medium rating, and **the `i–VII–VI–v` family at weight 2 is the INFERRED parameter** — the research names only the `i–v–i–VI` cycle the Stevie Wonder interpolation supplies, and the fourth family exists so the chord part clears the variety floor rather than because a record plays it. It is the first thing to delete. The gradual layer-addition intro is a 4–8 bar `intro` rule carrying `chords` alone.",
